{"id":"/docs-5","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#how-iggy-organizes-data","content":"Iggy uses a hierarchical model: streams contain topics, topics contain partitions, and partitions store messages in segments on disk. This gives you flexible multi-tenancy, parallel processing, and efficient storage all in one."},"8":{"id":"/docs-6","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#the-append-only-log","content":"Every partition is an append-only log. Messages are immutable once written, consumers can start from a chosen offset, and retained messages can be replayed. Retention removes old data, and offsets can contain gaps."},"9":{"id":"/docs-7","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"Capability"},"10":{"id":"/docs-8","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"Details"},"11":{"id":"/docs-9","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"Transport"},"12":{"id":"/docs-10","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"TCP, QUIC, WebSocket (custom binary protocol), HTTP (REST)"},"13":{"id":"/docs-11","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"Performance"},"14":{"id":"/docs-12","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"Thread-per-core + io_uring on Linux, binary message views, configurable memory pool with a default 4 GiB budget"},"15":{"id":"/docs-13","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"Security"},"16":{"id":"/docs-14","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"TLS on all transports, Argon2id hashing, AES-256-GCM message encryption, granular permissions with per-stream/per-topic permissions"},"17":{"id":"/docs-15","page_id":"/docs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs#key-capabilities","content":"Connectors"},"18":{"