ays disabled."},"3146":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-180","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"Opt-in trust of external token issuers for application-to-application authentication. With none configured, the listener accepts only self-issued tokens using the configured HMAC algorithm (HS256, HS384, or HS512)."},"3147":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-181","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"issuer, audience, and jwks_url are required per entry. user_id is the non-zero iggy user every token from that issuer is remapped onto. It defaults to 0 (root), which is rejected, so set it explicitly."},"3148":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-182","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"Enabling an issuer opens an outbound JWKS fetch that is reachable before a token's signature is verified: a token naming the issuer with an unknown key id can trigger a fetch to jwks_url. The target is fixed (not attacker-chosen), concurrent misses coalesce onto one fetch, and repeats are rate-limited to one outbound request per issuer per short window. The same window bounds how quickly a freshly rotated signing key is picked up."},"3149":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-183","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Key"},"3150":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-184","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Default"},"3151":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-185","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Description"},"3152":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-186","page_id":"/doc