{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-32","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"batch_size"},"4406":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-33","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"integer"},"4407":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-34","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"unused"},"4408":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-35","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Accepted but currently not read by the connector"},"4409":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-36","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"timeout_seconds"},"4410":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-37","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"integer"},"4411":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-38","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"30"},"4412":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-39","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"HTTP request timeout in seconds, from connection through response body; 0 is treated as 1"},"4413":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-40","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"The stream-level batch_length governs batching: each consume cycle submits its supported messages in one bulk request. The connector performs no retries of its own. Request, HTTP-status, and response-decoding failures return an error; the runtime logs and counts it, adds no processed messages for that batch, and continues polling. Consumer auto-commit occurs before indexing completes, and the failed poll is not replayed."},"4414":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-41","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Individual document errors inside a successful bulk response are logged and counted in the plugin's closing statistics, but the plugin still returns success. The runtime's processed-message count can therefore include documents rejected by Elasticsearch. Monitor the document-error logs as well as runtime errors."},"4415":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-42","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Bulk actions do not specify document IDs. Elasticsearch generates them, so replaying a message can create another document. The connector does not provide end-to-end exactly-once delivery."},"4416":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-43","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#index-mapping","content":"index_mapping is sent verbatim as the body of the create-index request, so it must be a structured object, not a JSON string embedded in TOML. It is used only when the connector creates an index; it does not update an existing index and is ignored when create_index_if_not_exists = false. That setting disables the startup existence check too. Express the mapping as nested TOML tables:"},"4417":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-44","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"JSON objects are indexed as documents directly. Other JSON values are forwarded without being wrapped as objects and can be rejected by Elasticsearch."},"4418":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-45","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Raw payloads are parsed as JSON when possible, and wrapped as { \"data\": \"<base64>\", \"data_type\": \"raw\" } when that fails."},"4419":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-46","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Text payloads are wrapped as { \"text\": \"...\", \"data_type\": \"text\" }."},"4420":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-47","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Other payload formats are skipped with a warning."},"4421":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-48","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Object documents are enriched before indexing with _iggy_offset, _iggy_stream, _iggy_topic, _iggy_partition, and _iggy_timestamp. These fields replace matching payload fields. _iggy_timestamp is the connector's processing time in Unix epoch milliseconds, not the message's stored timestamp. _iggy_headers is added or replaced only when message headers are present."},"4422":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-49","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Use HTTPS when credentials must be protected in transit. The connector uses the Elasticsearch client's certificate verification; this configuration does not expose a switch to disable it."},"4423":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"page","content":"HTTP Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http"},"4424":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","content":"Deliver messages from Iggy streams to any HTTP endpoint, from webhooks and REST APIs to serverless functions."},"4425":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"4426":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Common Options"},"4427":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"Batch Modes"},"4428":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"Metadata Envelope"},"4429":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#authentication","content":"Authentication"},"4430":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"Retry & Delivery Semantics"},"4431":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#example-configurations","content":"Example Configurations"},"4432":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-8","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#webhook-slack","content":"Webhook (Slack)"},"4433":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-9","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#bulk-rest-api-ingestion","content":"Bulk REST API Ingestion"},"4434":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-10","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#iot--sensor-relay-binary-payloads","content":"IoT / Sensor Relay (binary payloads)"},"4435":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-11","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#deployment--performance","content":"Deployment & Performance"},"4436":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-12","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"Known Limitations"},"4437":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-13","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","content":"The HTTP Sink connector consumes messages from Iggy streams and delivers them to any HTTP endpoint: webhooks, REST APIs, serverless functions, or SaaS integrations. This is the transport-level, generic HTTP connector. It's distinct from sinks such as Elasticsearch or Quickwit, which use HTTP internally to talk to one specific system. You bring the URL, headers, and batching strategy, and the sink handles transport, retries, and metadata wrapping."},"4438":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-14","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","content":"This page is a curated subset of the documentation. The canonical reference, including the full configuration table, deployment patterns, and performance analysis, is the upstream http_sink README in the apache/iggy repository."},"4439":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-15","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#configuration","content":"Use the broker credentials and runtime setup from the sink guide. From the matching 0.9.0/edge repository root, build the plugin:"},"4440":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-16","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#configuration","content":"For a local receiver, run this in a separate terminal:"},"4441":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-17","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#configuration","content":"Save this configuration in the runtime's connector directory:"},"4442":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-18","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#configuration","content":"Create the Iggy resources and send a JSON message, then start the connector runtime using the sink guide:"},"4443":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-19","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Option"},"4444":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-20","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Type"},"4445":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-21","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Default"},"4446":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-22","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Description"},"4447":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-23","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options"