lse"},"5165":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-52","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"Define a non-unique stream/topic/partition/offset index; requires metadata and only runs with automatic table definition"},"5166":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-53","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"batch_size"},"5167":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-54","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"u32"},"5168":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-55","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"1000"},"5169":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-56","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"Maximum input records per insert chunk; 0 is raised to 1"},"5170":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-57","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"payload_format"},"5171":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-58","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"string"},"5172":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-59","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"auto"},"5173":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-60","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"auto, json, text, base64, or binary (alias for base64)"},"5174":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-61","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"include_metadata"},"5175":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-62","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"bool"},"5176":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-63","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"true"},"5177":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-64","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"Store stream/topic/partition/offset/timestamp/schema fields"},"5178":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-65","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"The include_headers, include_checksum, and include_origin_timestamp flags also default to true and work independently of include_metadata. Retry and timeout options are query_timeout (30s per HTTP request), max_retries (3 total write attempts, with 0 raised to 1), retry_delay (100ms), and max_retry_delay (5s). Invalid duration strings log a warning and fall back to 1s; zero durations are accepted. The maximum delay is raised to the base delay if configured smaller. verbose_logging defaults to false and raises per-poll submission logs from debug to info. See the upstream surrealdb_sink README for the full table."},"5179":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-66","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"Namespace, database and table names must start with an ASCII letter or underscore and contain only ASCII letters, digits and underscores. Endpoint URLs cannot contain credentials, a path beyond /, a query or a fragment. An explicit http:// or https:// scheme takes precedence over use_tls. Payload-format and authentication-scope names are case-insensitive; unknown values prevent startup."},"5180":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-67","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"With root, namespace or database authentication, startup calls /signin and SQL requests use Basic authentication with the configured scope. Namespace/database users require pre-existing resources and auto_define_table = false. With auth_scope = \"none\", credentials are ignored; the server must permit those unauthenticated operations. Automatic DDL uses IF NOT EXISTS and does not migrate existing definitions. The optional <table>_iggy_offset_idx index is not a uniqueness constraint. define_indexes = true with metadata disabled rejects startup; without automatic DDL it only logs a warning and skips index creation."},"5181":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-68","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Every submitted record contains id, iggy_message_id, payload and payload_encoding. include_metadata adds iggy_stream, iggy_topic, iggy_partition_id, iggy_offset, iggy_timestamp and iggy_schema. The checksum and origin timestamp have separate flags. iggy_headers appears only when enabled and nonempty."},"5182":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-69","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Iggy message IDs, partition IDs, offsets, timestamps and checksums are stored as strings. Timestamps retain Iggy's microsecond values, not SurrealDB datetime values. Record IDs encode stream/topic UTF-8 bytes as hex, then append partition, offset and the 32-digit hexadecimal message ID. Changing the payload or transforms does not change that identity; changing any identity component creates a different key."},"5183":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-70","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Payload formatting operates after the runtime decoder and transforms:"},"5184":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-71","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"payload_format"},"5185":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-72","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Stored payload and encoding"},"5186":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-73","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"auto"},"5187":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-74","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"JSON values as json; text/Proto variants as text; raw/Avro/FlatBuffer bytes as base64, even when raw bytes contain valid JSON"},"5188":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-75","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"json"},"5189":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-76","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"A JSON value, parsing other payload variants as JSON; invalid JSON is rejected"},"5190":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-77","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"text"},"5191":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-78","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"A string, decoding other payload bytes as UTF-8; invalid UTF-8 is rejected"},"5192":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-79","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"base64 / binary"},"5193":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-80","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Base64 of the payload bytes, with payload_encoding = \"base64\""},"5194":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-81","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"Non-raw headers are stored as strings, including numbers and booleans. Raw headers use {\"data\":\"AQID\",\"iggy_header_encoding\":\"base64\"}. Payload JSON is sent as SurrealQL values, so destination schema, numeric and other value constraints still apply."},"5195":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-82","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#delivery-semantics","content":"The runtime auto-commits while polling, logs/counts plugin callback failures, and continues without replaying the failed batch. The sink retries transaction-conflict errors, connection/timeouts, and HTTP 408, 429, 500, 502, 503 and 504. Delays use capped exponential backoff with jitter; Retry-After is not used. Connection errors trigger reconnection and repeat sign-in/health/optional DDL. A failed reconnect stops that chunk, and retries plus startup requests can exceed query_timeout in total."},"5196":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-83","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#delivery-semantics","content":"A malformed record is skipped while valid records in its chunk are still submitted. A failed chunk does not stop later chunks, and the last error is returned. The sink checks HTTP and SQL statement statuses. Its own processed counter counts records submitted in successful statements, including records ignored by INSERT IGNORE; runtime counters instead reflect whether the whole callback succeeded. Neither is a count of newly inserted rows."},"5197":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-84","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#delivery-semantics","content":"SurrealQL INSERT IGNORE preserves existing records with the same ID, including their old payloads. With the SurrealDB 3.1.4 instance above, IGNORE also silently skips unique-index conflicts and field-assertion failures while accepting valid records from the same chunk. These skips return a successful statement and are included in processed counters. This protects repeated writes of the same identities; it does not ensure that a failed batch will be delivered. There is no end-to-end at-least-once guarantee."},"5198":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-85","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#transforms","content":"Transforms can be applied before writing to SurrealDB. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."},"5199":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","type":"page","content":"Elasticsearch Source","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch"},"5200":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","content":"Poll documents from an Elasticsearch index into Iggy streams, incrementally when a timestamp field is configured."},"5201":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"5202":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Plugin config options"},"5203":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#how-polling-works","content":"How Polling Works"},"5204":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#state","content":"State"},"5205":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","content":"The Elasticsearch source connector polls documents from an Elasticsearch index and produces them to Iggy streams. With a timestamp field configured, it filters searches using the last acknowledged timestamp. This is a timestamp watermark, with the limitations described below."},"5206":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#configuration","content":"Use the broker credentials and main runtime configuration from the source guide. From the matching 0.9.0/edge Iggy checkout root, build the plugin:"},"5207":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#configuration","content":"For this local example, start Elasticsearch with aut