sword for auto-login"},"5815":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-157","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#autologinsettings","content":"PersonalAccessToken"},"5816":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-158","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#autologinsettings","content":"string"},"5817":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-159","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#autologinsettings","content":"\"\""},"5818":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-160","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#autologinsettings","content":"Personal access token to sign in with instead of a username and password; takes precedence over them when set"},"5819":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-161","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#autologinsettings","content":"All properties are init-only: build the settings with an object initializer or the static factories AutoLoginSettings.For(username, password) and AutoLoginSettings.ForPersonalAccessToken(token). TCP reconnects use configured auto-login credentials first, then credentials remembered from a successful manual login. Without either, a reconnect cannot restore the authenticated session."},"5820":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-162","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#message-encryption","content":"Set IggyClientConfigurator.MessageEncryptor to encrypt message payloads and user headers client-side. They are encrypted on send and decrypted on poll; routing information and message metadata remain visible to the server. The built-in AesMessageEncryptor uses AES-GCM (confidentiality + authenticity) and takes a 16-, 24-, or 32-byte key for AES-128/192/256:"},"5821":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-163","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#message-encryption","content":"Keep the same key for clients that exchange encrypted messages and for later reads; the generated key above lasts only for this example. For a custom scheme, implement IMessageEncryptor."},"5822":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-164","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#message-encryption","content":"Things to know:"},"5823":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-165","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#message-encryption","content":"The encryptor applies to every message on the connection - topics mixing encrypted and plaintext messages are not supported."},"5824":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-166","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#message-encryption","content":"You own the encryptor and must dispose it once the client is done with it."},"5825":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-167","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#message-encryption","content":"With an encryptor configured, polling with autoCommit: true throws InvalidOperationException by default: the server commits the offset before the client decrypts, so a decryption failure would silently skip the whole batch. Poll with autoCommit: false and store offsets after processing, or opt in with AllowAutoCommitWithEncryptor = true. IggyConsumer separately rejects wire auto-commit with encryption; use AfterReceive or Disabled there."},"5826":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-168","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#message-encryption","content":"On the high-level builders, WithEncryptor(...) is only valid when the builder creates its own client; for an external client, set MessageEncryptor on the configurator instead."},"5827":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-169","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#connection-events","content":"TCP clients publish connection state changes, useful for reacting to reconnects. HTTP subscription methods are no-ops:"},"5828":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-170","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#identifiers","content":"Streams, topics, users, and consumer groups are referenced by an Identifier, which can be either numeric or a name:"},"5829":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-171","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#identifiers","content":"Server-assigned ids are 0-based: the first stream, topic, partition, or consumer group gets id 0. The root user has id 0 as well."},"5830":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-172","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#user-login","content":"Use the credentials configured when the server was initialized. These examples use the iggy / iggy setup from the introduction:"},"5831":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-173","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#creating-users","content":"Create new users with customizable permissions:"},"5832":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-174","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#creating-users","content":"Besides Global, Permissions.Streams scopes permissions to specific streams (keyed by numeric stream id), and each StreamPermissions can in turn scope down to specific topics:"},"5833":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-175","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#personal-access-tokens","content":"Create and use Personal Access Tokens (PAT) for programmatic access:"},"5834":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-176","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#topics","content":"Every stream contains topics that organize messages into partitions:"},"5835":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-177","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#topics","content":"compressionAlgorithm, messageExpiry, and maxTopicSize are optional. messageExpiry is a nullable TimeSpan."},"5836":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-178","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#topic-options","content":"CreateTopicAsync also accepts an options dictionary for settings that have no parameter of their own. Build it with the TopicOptions helper (in Apache.Iggy.Contracts):"},"5837":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-179","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#topic-options","content":"Nullable properties left null emit no key and keep the server default. Durability and ConsumerOffsetDurability are non-nullable, default independently to Replicated, and are always emitted by ToDictionary(). These keys are settable at creation only: UpdateTopicAsync refuses them by name, the same way it refuses a key outside the server's catalog, so a mistyped key fails the call instead of being silently ignored. Use DescribeOptionsAsync to enumerate the keys a server accepts."},"5838":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-180","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#topic-options","content":"There is no on-demand flush command. Durability controls message completion and ConsumerOffsetDurability controls explicit offset-store completion. Persisted waits for persistence on the required quorum; flush thresholds alone do not provide that guarantee. See Durability and Topic options."},"5839":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-181","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#topic-options","content":"TCP omits zero expiry/size defaults from a topic update; HTTP sends them. Use explicit values when updating retention and review the default-sentinel caveat."},"5840":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-182","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#partitions","content":"Add partitions to or remove them from an existing topic:"},"5841":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-183","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#sending-messages","content":"A Message takes an id (Guid or UInt128) and a payload:"},"5842":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-184","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#sending-messages","content":"SendMessagesAsync returns a SendMessagesResponse whose Confirmations carry StreamId, TopicId, PartitionId, and BaseOffset (the offset of the first message of the batch) per committed batch. An empty list reports no assigned offsets. A single-message overload is also available: SendMessagesAsync(streamId, topicId, partitioning, message)."},"5843":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-185","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#sending-messages","content":"To send many payloads without a byte[] allocation per message, build them into a single pooled buffer with RentedMessageBatchBuilder - see Publishing with rented batches."},"5844":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-186","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#partitioning-strategies","content":"Control which partition receives each message:"},"5845":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-187","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#partitioning-strategies","content":"Partition selection is resolved client-side on both transports. Balanced partitioning round-robins over the topic's partitions, and key-based routing hashes the key with xxHash32 modulo the partition count, consistent with the Rust SDK for the same encoded key bytes and partition count. Strings use UTF-8, integers use little-endian bytes, and GUID keys use Guid.ToByteArray()."},"5846":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-188","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#user-defined-headers","content":"Add typed custom headers to messages. Build keys with HeaderKey.FromString and values with the HeaderValue.From* factories:"},"5847":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-189","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#user-defined-headers","content":"Available value factories: FromString, FromBool, FromBytes, FromUInt8, FromInt32, FromInt64, FromInt128, FromUInt32, FromUInt64, FromUInt128, FromFloat, FromDouble, FromGuid."},"5848":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-190","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#fetching-messages","content":"Poll a batch of messages. A null partitionId selects partition 0 for an ordinary consumer. For a group consumer, null lets the TCP client rotate through its assigned partitions:"},"5849":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-191","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#fetching-messages","content":"A convenience overload accepts a MessageFetchRequest if you prefer named fields:"},"5850":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-192","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#fetching-messages","content":"With autoCommit: true, the server advances/submits the offset before application processing; the poll reply does not wait for durable completion of that offset store. Use autoCommit: false and explicitly store offsets after processing when that distinction matters."},"5851":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-193","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"On TCP, PollMessagesAsync copies each payload into its own byte[]. PollMessagesRentedAsync instead returns a PolledMessagesRental whose payloads and raw headers share a pooled buffer. Message wrappers and lazily parsed headers still allocate. HTTP first materializes its JSON response and then adapts it to the rental API."},"5852":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-194","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"The rental owns that buffer, so you must dispose it, and the payload/header memory is only valid until you do. Wrap it in using and never hold a Payload/RawUserHeaders reference past the block:"},"5853":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-195","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"A MessageFetchRequest overload (PollMessagesRentedAsync(request)) is also available."},"5854":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-196","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"PolledMessagesRental (IDisposable) exposes:"},"5855":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-197","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Member"},"5856":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-198","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Type"},"5857":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-199","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Description"},"5858":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-200","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"PartitionId"},"5859":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-201","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"uint"},"5860":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-202","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Partition the messages came from"},"5861":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-203","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"CurrentOffset"},"5862":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-204","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"ulong"},"5863":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-205","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Current offset for the partition"},"5864":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-206","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Messages"},"5865":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-207","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"IReadOnlyList<RentedMessageResponse>"},"5866":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-208","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"The rented messages"},"5867":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-209","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Each RentedMessageResponse:"},"5868":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-210","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Member"},"5869":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-211","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Type"},"5870":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-212","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Description"},"5871":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-213","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Header"},"5872":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-214","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"MessageHeader"},"5873":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-215","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Message header (offset, timestamp, id, …)"},"5874":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-216","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Payload"},"5875":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-217","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"ReadOnlyMemory<byte>"},"5876":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-218","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Payload backed by rented memory - valid only until the rental is disposed"},"5877":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-219","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"RawUserHeaders"},"5878":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-220","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"ReadOnlyMemory<byte>"},"5879":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-221","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Raw user-header bytes backed by rented memory"},"5880":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-222","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"UserHeaders"},"5881":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-223","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Dictionary<HeaderKey, HeaderValue>?"},"5882":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-224","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"User headers, parsed lazily and cached on first access"},"5883":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-225","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"Warning: Do not store Payload, RawUserHeaders, or a RentedMessageResponse beyond the using scope. To retain data, copy it out (e.g. message.Payload.ToArray()) before disposal."},"5884":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-226","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-with-rented-buffers","content":"The high-level IggyConsumer exposes the same pooled path as an async stream via ReceiveRentedAsync - see Consuming with rented buffers."},"5885":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-227","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#polling-strategies","content":"Control where consumption starts:"},"5886":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-228","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#offset-management","content":"Consumer offsets are keyed by consumer + stream + topic + partition. Note the argument order - the Consumer comes first:"},"5887":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-229","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#consumer-groups","content":"Consumer groups coordinate message consumption across multiple consumers, load-balancing partitions between members."},"5888":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-230","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#joining-and-leaving","content":"Note: Join/Leave are TCP-only and throw FeatureUnavailableException on HTTP."},"5889":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-231","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#system-operations","content":"PingAsync is more than a bare ping over TCP: it also re-syncs the assignment of every consumer group this client has joined, at the cost of one extra round trip per joined group. The client already pings on its own every HeartbeatInterval, so an explicit ping is only needed to force an assignment refresh sooner. GetCurrentAddress() is useful under leader redirection, when the client may have followed the cluster roster to a different node than the one it was configured with (see Connection semantics)."},"5890":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-232","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#option-catalog","content":"DescribeOptionsAsync enumerates the option keys a server accepts for a resource scope (OptionsScope.Topic, OptionsScope.Stream, or OptionsScope.User), with the kind, default, and description of each. This is the discovery surface for the topic options dictionary:"},"5891":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-233","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#raw-binary-requests","content":"SendBinaryRequestAsync is an escape hatch that sends a raw command code with a prebuilt payload and returns the raw response bytes, for commands the typed API does not cover:"},"5892":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-234","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#raw-binary-requests","content":"Session-control codes (login, logout, and the like) are rejected with an invalid-command error, and the operation is TCP-only: HTTP clients throw FeatureUnavailableException."},"5893":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-235","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#snapshots","content":"Capture a system snapshot as a compressed archive:"},"5894":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-236","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#snapshots","content":"Compression methods: Stored, Deflated, Bzip2, Zstd, Lzma, Xz.\nSnapshot types: FilesystemOverview, ProcessList, ResourceUsage, Test, ServerLogs, ServerConfig, All."},"5895":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-237","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#snapshots","content":"A full snapshot can exceed the default 64 MiB reply-frame bound, in which case the reply is refused and the connection dropped. Raise MaxResponseFrameSize before requesting large snapshots."},"5896":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-238","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#segment-management","content":"Delete up to N of the oldest sealed segments from a partition. The active segment is retained:"},"5897":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide-239","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/guide#segment-management","content":"Note: TCP-only - throws FeatureUnavailableException on HTTP."},"5898":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","type":"page","content":"High-level SDK","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","C#"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk"},"5899":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","content":"IggyPublisher and IggyConsumer for C#, with background batching, retries and automatic offset commits."},"5900":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk#iggypublisher","content":"IggyPublisher"},"5901":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/high-level-sdk-