d in the background"],[6400,"Every d, plus at the after trigger"],[6398,"Every d, plus at the when trigger"],[4776,"Every document has a generated _id of stream:topic:partition:message_id and a payload field. The offset is not part of the ID. Payload fields remain nested under payload, so a payload's own _id does not replace the connector's ID. Message headers are not stored."],[1549,"Every duration must be nonzero. The 0, disabled, and unlimited sentinels all parse to a zero duration and are rejected. There's no way to switch the liveness window off."],[1259,"Every iggy CLI command with its arguments, flags, and a runnable example"],[1286,"Every list command accepts -l, --list-mode <table|list> (default: table)."],[691,"Every message on a binary transport is a fixed 256-byte header followed by an optional body. The header is a #[repr(C)] struct decoded by pointer cast (zero-copy), so field offsets are fixed and enforced at compile time in the server. Three header shapes cross the client boundary:"],[232,"Every node in [[cluster.nodes]] exposes a tcp_replica port next to the client ports: ports = { tcp = 8090, quic = 8080, http = 3000, websocket = 8092, tcp_replica = 9090 }. The node's ip is the roster address for the replica plane (clients fall back to it when advertised_address is unset)."],[1599,"Every node loads the same configuration. Nodes are told apart only by --replica-id, which selects that node's own entry in the cluster.nodes roster."],[8,"Every partition is an append-only log. Messages are immutable once written, consumers can start from a chosen offset, and retained messages can be replayed. Retention removes old data, and offsets can contain gaps."],[3847,"Every request and reply on the stateful transports starts with a fixed 256-byte header (the same Viewstamped Replication header layout the cluster uses internally), followed by the command payload. The iggy_binary_protocol crate provides zero-copy serialization for these headers, and foreign SDKs implement the same contract natively. See the Binary Protocol section for the full specification."],[1614,"Every roster field can be provided through typed environment variables instead of TOML, which suits container deployments:"],[1459,"Every SDK speaks the VSR wire protocol and can connect to any node of a cluster. Client-side leader redirection is exercised by the shared leader_redirection BDD suite, which runs against a real two-node cluster:"],[6347,"Every send method returns a SendMessagesResponse carrying the commit confirmations of the chunks the send was split into. The list is empty whenever the server sends no confirmation payload, and always for a background producer, which hands the messages to a dispatcher and returns before the send happens. Branch on confirmations.is_empty() instead of indexing. A retried chunk may already have been committed by an earlier attempt, so a confirmation offset does not imply uniqueness. Direct-send completion follows the topic's durability policy."],[5834,"Every stream contains topics that organize messages into partitions:"],[5181,"Every submitted record contains id, iggy_message_id, payload and payload_encoding. include_metadata adds iggy_stream, iggy_topic, iggy_partition_id, iggy_offset, iggy_timestamp and iggy_schema. The checksum and origin timestamp have separate flags. iggy_headers appears only when enabled and nonempty."],[3462,"evicted_ring_bytes_max"],[3459,"evicted_ring_capacity"],[283,"Eviction"],[708,"Eviction"],[1100,"Eviction reason, see below."],[1101,"Eviction reasons:"],[690,"EvictionHeader"],[694,"EvictionHeader: server to client, session-terminal rejection with no body."],[1317,"Exactly one polling strategy is required:"],[4431,"Example Configurations"],[5589,"Examples"],[5618,"Examples"],[5636,"Examples"],[6105,"Examples"],[6134,"Examples"],[6149,"Examples"],[6179,"Examples"],[6214,"Examples"],[6237,"Examples"],[6255,"Examples"],[6268,"Examples"],[6104,"Examples - producer, consumer-group, and typed-